 "statement": "Annotated from the Beinecke scan alone (full page at 1900 pixels). A wheel with a dark green four-legged animal at the centre, long-snouted, its tail curled up in a loop, a yellow star tethered above it and a word in a different script beneath. Around it are an inner and an outer ring of nude female figures standing with their feet toward the centre, without tubs, each holding a yellow star on a line and each with a short label; four more such figures stand in a row on top of the wheel, outside the outer text ring. The label groups in the transcription have 4, 16 and 10 lines; I matched them to the four figures on top (left to right), the outer ring and the inner ring. The four on top are a clear count; my own counts of the two rings agree with sixteen and ten to within one. Ring labels were paired clockwise from twelve o'clock, an assumption about starting point and direction, so each ring's pairing may be rotated. Per-figure features are recorded individually for the four top figures and are generic for the rings.",
